Creating Arrays
-We can create arrays by using array( ) function in Numpy.
first time - pip install numpy.

Eg.
---
import numpy as np
a=[2,4,5,6,3,3]
arr=np.array(a)
print(arr)

Output
-----
[2 4 5 6 3 3]


List vs numpy
=============
List- output- [2,4,5,6,3,3]
Nump output- [2 4 5 6 3 3]

Method                    Code Example
From a list               np.array([1,2,3])
Multi-dim array           np.array([[1,2,3], [4,5,6]])
Array of zeros            np.zeros((2,3))
Array of ones             np.ones((2,3))
Range of numbers          np.arange(0, 10, 2)
Evenly spaced numbers     np.linspace(0, 1, 5)
Fill Specific Element     np.full((2,3), 6)
For Identity Matrix       np.eye(3)
